# One target/ for the whole lane — see Cargo.toml.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. `/target` would cover only the workspace root's, and a
# stray per-relic target/ — a leftover from before the workspace, or a member
# built with an overridden target-dir — would go unignored and be staged. There
# is no tracked path named target/ at any depth, so the broad rule costs nothing.
target/

# cargo-mutants' report tree, and the copy it rotates on the next run.
# `relic mutants` is part of the verification standard, so this is written by a
# sanctioned command rather than by accident — and it is 4 MiB of logs per run,
# regenerated whole. Undeclared, it reported itself as several hundred
# undecided paths in `assay`'s yadm-coverage station.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
